{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"CLSA-2026-1782314022","published":"2026-06-24T15:14:03Z","modified":"2026-10-26T09:32:03.566907006Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-46559","CVE-2026-46692","CVE-2026-46693","CVE-2026-47166"],"summary":"Fix CVE(s): CVE-2026-46559, CVE-2026-46692, CVE-2026-46693, CVE-2026-47166","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap over-write, file-descriptor hijack race, and heap\n     over-read in the distributed pixel cache server\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-46692-46693-47166.patch: bound the requested\n       region against the pixel cache extent before reading or writing pixels\n       and indexes, and hand each connection a private heap-allocated socket to\n       a detached handler thread in magick/distribute-cache.c\n     - CVE-2026-46692\n     - CVE-2026-46693\n     - CVE-2026-47166\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap buffer over-write of a single byte in the JP2\n     encoder via crafted jp2:quality / jp2:rate options\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-46559.patch: bound the jp2:quality and jp2:rate\n       parse loops by the tcp_distoratio/tcp_rates array extent in\n       WriteJP2Image() in coders/jp2.c (defense-in-depth; the JP2 coder is not\n       compiled in this build)\n     - CVE-2026-46559","affected":[{"package":{"name":"imagemagick","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:18.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/imagemagick?distro=ubuntu-18.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8:6.9.7.4+dfsg-16ubuntu6.15+tuxcare.els38"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/ubuntu18.04els/CLSA-2026-1782314022.json"}},{"package":{"name":"imagemagick-6-common","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:18.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/imagemagick-6-common?distro=ubuntu-18.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8:6.9.7.4+dfsg-16ubuntu6.15+tuxcare.els38"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/ubuntu18.04els/CLSA-2026-